                        "sense_id": "7c9c7296-3ba8-396d-a859-fd12a5276c65",
                        "entry_id": "963b4531-a84a-3a01-baa4-ab121c037fd7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The color of gingerline: orangish brown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb2c50a0-a288-4644-8629-f2f1a7db6820",
                                "sense_id": "7c9c7296-3ba8-396d-a859-fd12a5276c65",
                                "text": "Four of them can now be dyed without increase, French green, gingerline, deer colour, orange colour."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58ea0032-489c-4a20-a696-128f4c5c61c9",
                                "sense_id": "7c9c7296-3ba8-396d-a859-fd12a5276c65",
                                "text": "Silk grogans, satins, velvet fine, The rosy-colour'd carnadine, Your nutmeg hue, or gingerline, Cloth-of-tissue or tabine, That like beaten gold will shine In your amorous ladies' eyne, Whilst you their softer silks do twine?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f416fb2a-cbe6-478e-b72a-ed6f53fb30e5",
                                "sense_id": "7c9c7296-3ba8-396d-a859-fd12a5276c65",
                                "text": "Some wore great wide gallyslops down to the knee, others bombasted trunk hose with canions, while all, without exception, were paned and slashed, fringed and embroidered in the most brilliant colours, pearl white, primrose, carnation, gingerline, and the richest fabrics: satins, velvets, damasks and brocades all newly come from the tailor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d331c8ec-f369-453a-927a-b943259267ec",
                                "sense_id": "7c9c7296-3ba8-396d-a859-fd12a5276c65",
                                "text": "Colors that reflected England's new colonies and recent explorations; brick, greediline, gingerline, muske, pepper, grape, fawne, sage, corke, tobacco, Virginia-ffrog."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
